   "posture": "supine, upper limbs in anatomical position",
   "task": "static"
  },
  "equations": [],
  "subject_model": null,
  "notes": "Vertebral-level segments bounded through the intervertebral discs (each contains one complete vertebral body); upper (thorax) = T1-T12, middle (abdomen) = L1-L5, lower (pelvis) = S1-S5 (pubic symphysis); trunk = T1-S5. Neck and upper limbs (lateral to glenohumeral joint) and lower limbs (lateral to hip joint) excluded. NOTE: these boundaries differ fundamentally from Pearsall 1994/Zatsiorsky/de Leva (landmark-based) trunk subsegments."
 },
